{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And he said, lest you and your household come to poverty.</b> Out of honor, for to his brothers he said, \"For Elohim sent me before you to preserve life\" and \"to make for you a remnant,\" for they were about to die and no remnant would be left to them, but to his father he did not wish to say so. And he said that if you remain in the land of Canaan — you will come to poverty, for I will not be able to send you bread in abundance from the king's treasuries to the land of Canaan, for they will suspect me of selling it there to make for myself there stores of silver and to return to my land and to my birthplace, but when you come and they know that you are my father and my brother, the king will give me permission."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:44:58.659682162Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}